---
import PolicyLayout from '@/components/policy/PolicyLayout.astro';
import { fetchGlobal } from '@/lib/global';

const global = await fetchGlobal();
const email = global?.generalEmail ?? 'externalaffairs@empower.org.ki';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  subtitle="How we collect, manage, use, and safeguard information obtained through our website, digital programs, and infrastructure."
  description="How Empower Kiribati collects, uses, and safeguards personal information under the Kiribati Data Protection Act 2025, and how to make a privacy request."
>
  <h2>1. Overview &amp; Commitment</h2>
  <p>
    As a digital-first social impact organization, we recognize that data security is not merely a
    technical requirement, but a fundamental pillar of our commitment to safeguarding and human
    rights. We promote safe practices across our organization to model excellence in digital safety,
    safeguard access to personal and organizational data, and protect the security and privacy of
    all data subjects.
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy sets out how we collect, manage, use, and safeguard information obtained through our
    website, digital programs, and infrastructure.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information Collection &amp; Usage</h2>
  <p>We adhere strictly to principles of purpose limitation and data minimization across all operations.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Purpose Limitation:</strong> Any identifiable participant information we collect is kept
      secure and used exclusively for the specific purpose for which it was originally collected.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Data Minimization:</strong> Our roles are explicitly restricted to collecting only the
      participant data strictly required to fulfill a given project's defined objective.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Transparency Exclusion:</strong> Personal identifiable participant data is strictly excluded
      from our standard transparency practices to preserve individual privacy.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Protection of Children &amp; Vulnerable Participants</h2>
  <p>
    We maintain a dedicated framework to protect the welfare, rights, and privacy of children, youth,
    women, and other vulnerable groups in all digital and physical environments.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Data Collection Limits for Minors:</strong> Personal data for individuals under the age of
      18 or those otherwise lacking legal capacity can only be collected for the specific purposes of
      educational programs and for no other reason.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Encrypted Domain Storage:</strong> Notwithstanding standard operational transparency, all
      sensitive records and personal data concerning vulnerable persons must be stored within a
      dedicated Encrypted Domain.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Safeguarding &amp; International Alignment:</strong> All digital handling of participant
      data must comply with international conventions, our
      <a href="/safety-of-vulnerable-persons">Safety of Vulnerable Persons</a> policy, and Kiribati
      national child welfare and family protection legislation.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Anonymization &amp; Public Reporting</h2>
  <p>To balance public accountability with individual privacy, we enforce systematic data anonymization.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Public Impact Metrics:</strong> Any data compiled for public impact reporting, program
      evaluation, or general communications must be rendered fully anonymous prior to publication.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Re-identification Safeguards:</strong> Our anonymization processes are designed to
      guarantee that no individual data subject can be re-identified from general metrics or shared
      reports.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Data Security &amp; Cybersafety Standards</h2>
  <p>
    All partners, contractors, and volunteers performing accountabilities on our behalf are subject
    to rigorous technical and operational security controls.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Eligibility &amp; Access Control:</strong> Digital access is granted strictly on a
      role-accountability basis. All role fillers must complete our mandatory Cybersafety Induction
      learning program prior to access authorization.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Authentication &amp; Password Hygiene:</strong> Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) is
      mandatory for all of our accounts, including email, shared workspace platforms, and data
      repositories. Password reuse across our systems is strictly forbidden, and all credentials must
      be generated and stored using our designated password manager.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Device Protection:</strong> Any physical device used to fulfill accountabilities on our
      behalf is required to run an approved virus protection software.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Third-Party Software Review:</strong> Our Technology Steward must conduct a mandatory
      security review of any proposed new software or digital tool to verify that the provider meets
      our privacy standards.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Incident Response &amp; Breach Notification</h2>
  <p>
    We maintain active incident detection and swift escalation protocols to address any potential
    security compromises.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Internal Escalation Window:</strong> If a partner suspects a data breach, loses a device
      containing our data, or receives a suspicious message, they must report the incident directly to
      the Technology Steward within 2 to 4 hours rather than waiting for standard meeting cycles.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Transparent Communication:</strong> In the event of a confirmed data leak or breach, we
      prioritize immediate transparency with affected individuals.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal Alignment:</strong> Our incident mitigation and notification protocols operate in
      full compliance with the Kiribati Data Protection Act 2025 and international data protection
      standards.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Data Subject Rights &amp; Inquiries</h2>
  <p>
    Data subjects maintain full rights regarding the personal data we process, in accordance with the
    Data Protection Act 2025.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Rights of Access &amp; Rectification:</strong> Data subjects have the right to request
      access to, correction of, or deletion of the personal information we maintain.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Privacy Inquiries &amp; Escalations:</strong> For privacy requests, data access inquiries,
      or to submit a security concern, data subjects and website visitors may contact us at
      <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
</PolicyLayout>
